# Host tests — no pack-name contracts

Parent: [pack-product host](./forja-pack-product-host.mdc) · skill **forja-pack-product-host**

Packs are external. Host tests prove **generic** contracts only — never that a shipped hub/provider id exists.

---

## Forbidden in `apps/forja/test/**`

| Do not | Why |
|--------|-----|
| Assert a **shipped plugin id** exists in manifest (`kisskh`, `videasy`, `hianime`, …) | Pack inventory |
| Assert **hub slot / tab ids** as behavioral contracts (`anime`, `asian_drama`, `arabic`) | User may ship `my_hub` |
| Use `loadAllForjaHqPlugins()` / repo pack tree as **oracle** for categories/registry/panel | Couples CI to one tree |
| Hardcode pack **type tokens** from real manifests | Types come from manifest |
| Test “does our anime hub work” in the Flutter suite | Pack tests / manual QA |

**Wrong:** `expect(byId('kisskh').types, ['drama'])` after loading providers manifest.  
**Right:** `EnginePlugin.fromJson({'id': 'test-provider-a', 'types': ['foo']})` → generic helper → `'foo'`.

---

## Allowed

- Synthetic fixtures — arbitrary ids (`test-provider-a`), type tokens (`foo`, `movie`)
- Generic mechanics — `forjaHqSlot('…/hubs/any_slot/manifest.json')` → `'any_slot'`
- Structural constants only when testing the constant itself
- Opaque passthrough — no claim the token is a real shipped hub

## Where pack contract tests go

| Layer | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Provider JS / upstream / inventory | pack CI / env-gated pack tests |
| Host generic contracts | `apps/forja/test/**` + synthetic fixtures |

Grep new host tests for shipped plugin ids and hub slot names. If uninstall/rename would break the assertion, it does not belong here.
